  "notes": "Two MSRVs (PCV-001-0019, PCV-001-0179) found out of TS band during post-outage bench testing; valves remained capable of performing safety function throughout, no automatic/manual safety system responses occurred, and no SSC inoperability contributed to the event. Event is a TS-prohibited-condition report (50.73(a)(2)(i)(B)), not an equipment operability loss; consequence modeled as regulatory/TS noncompliance rather than a system-inoperable window. MSRV Automatic Actuation Logic is explicitly described as providing defense-in-depth during a pressure transient (not stated as 'operable throughout event' in the strict BACKED_UP_BY sense, but narrative frames it as an available independent function) - retained per analysis section language. Seven previous similar LERs listed; only titles/plant/unit inferred from cycle references, exact report titles not given verbatim in narrative."
